# mesa-nvk-horizon — versions.
#
# Plain KEY=value, sourceable by any POSIX shell. No absolute paths from
# any developer's machine (scripts/check-no-abs-paths.sh enforces this):
# host-side locations are resolved at run time through $DEVKITPRO or
# $PWD, and the only absolute paths named here are *inside* the
# container image.
#
# THE FILE HAS TWO HALVES:
#
#   ENVIRONMENT — how to *reach* the Switch toolchain. Nothing about its
#                 contents is recorded, checked or updated here.
#   PINNED      — the inputs this project chooses. Changing one is a
#                 decision.
#
# Copyright (c) mesa-nvk-horizon contributors
# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT

# =====================================================================
# ENVIRONMENT — the Switch toolchain, taken as given
# =====================================================================
# Policy (owner's decision, 2026-07-26): **libnx and the rest of the
# Switch toolchain belong to the environment, not to this project.**
# They are neither pinned nor updated from here. Whatever `$DEVKITPRO`
# points at, or whatever is inside the container image the developer
# runs, is what gets used.
#
# Why this is the right split, and not laziness: libnx gains fixes and
# new `nv`-service bindings frequently, and this backend is written
# against exactly those services. A version recorded in this file could
# only ever be a stale copy of a fact that lives somewhere else — and a
# misleading one, because the image builds libnx from git HEAD on top of
# the package, so `dkp-pacman -Q libnx` describes only 21 of its 226
# installed files (measured: `dkp-pacman -Qkk libnx` reports 205
# altered). Updating libnx is `dkp-pacman -Syu`, or a newer image. It is
# not an edit to this repository.
#
# What this project does instead of tracking versions is *record what it
# actually used*: scripts/package-horizon.sh writes the resolved image
# digest and the live package versions into build/pkg/MANIFEST.txt next
# to each artefact's sha256, so a result measured on console stays
# attributable to a specific build. Reading, never pinning.
#
# Report what the current environment provides:
#   scripts/print-toolchain-versions.sh

# Used only when $DEVKITPRO is unset, as the fallback toolchain
# (CLAUDE.md). Override with HORIZON_NX_IMAGE=<any reference> to build
# against a different environment — including a specific digest, when
# reproducing the artefacts behind a recorded hardware run.
HORIZON_NX_IMAGE_REPO=ghcr.io/d3fau4/nx-dev
HORIZON_NX_IMAGE_TAG=latest

# devkitPro install prefix *inside* that image. Recorded so no script
# types the path inline; it is a property of the image's layout, not a
# version.
HORIZON_NX_IMAGE_DEVKITPRO=/opt/devkitpro

# The image scripts/build-toolchain-image.sh produces from the one
# above by adding libclang, bindgen, cbindgen and the Rust sysroot
# (toolchain/Dockerfile). It is local to the machine that built it —
# nothing pushes or pulls it — and it is used only when it exists, so
# every build from before Phase 4 keeps running against the base image
# unchanged. The tag tracks the base image's, because the layer is only
# meaningful on top of that base.
HORIZON_NX_DERIVED_REPO=mesa-nvk-horizon/nx-dev-mesa

# Where that image puts what it adds. Properties of its layout, like
# HORIZON_NX_IMAGE_DEVKITPRO above, named here so neither the
# Dockerfile nor the scripts type them inline.
HORIZON_IMAGE_RUST_TOOLS_BIN=/opt/rust-tools/bin
HORIZON_IMAGE_RUST_SYSROOT=/opt/rust-sysroot

# The three directories the build resolves bare tool names from — the
# Meson cross file lists its [binaries] unqualified on purpose, so all
# of them have to be on PATH.
#
# Each was found missing in a different mode, which is why all three are
# listed explicitly rather than assumed:
#   - the image's PATH omits devkitA64/bin (it lists tools/bin,
#     devkitARM/bin and devkitPPC/bin), so the cross compiler is not
#     found in a plain `docker run ... sh -c`;
#   - a local devkitPro needs tools/bin adding as well, for elf2nro and
#     nacptool. The image's PATH already had that one, which masked it
#     until the local path was actually exercised;
#   - portlibs/switch/bin holds aarch64-none-elf-pkg-config, devkitPro's
#     wrapper that points pkg-config at the Switch portlibs and nothing
#     else. Without it on PATH the cross file's `pkg-config` binary does
#     not resolve, every dependency() lookup silently finds nothing, and
#     Mesa falls through to downloading wrap subprojects — which cannot
#     work, since containers here have no network. Found by configuring
#     Mesa: zlib is installed in portlibs (zlib.pc reports 1.3.1) and
#     was still being fetched from zlib.net.
HORIZON_TOOLCHAIN_BINDIR_REL=devkitA64/bin
HORIZON_TOOLS_BINDIR_REL=tools/bin
HORIZON_PORTLIBS_BINDIR_REL=portlibs/switch/bin

# Stable properties of the devkitA64 cross toolchain. These are what the
# build actually depends on, and unlike package versions they do not
# move when the environment is updated.
DEVKITA64_TARGET_TRIPLE=aarch64-none-elf
DEVKITA64_TOOL_PREFIX=aarch64-none-elf-

# Where rustup lives inside the image. The image installs the rolling
# `nightly` with rust-src; which nightly, like libnx, is the
# environment's business (docs/rust-toolchain.md).
RUST_CARGO_HOME_IN_IMAGE=/opt/cargo

# =====================================================================
# PINNED — changing these is a decision, not an update
# =====================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mesa (decision D2)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Current stable series at Phase 2 start. Chosen over the reference
# port's 25.0.7 for a modern nvkmd surface and a credible upstreaming
# path (docs/known-risks.md R14).
#
# Pinned, unlike the Switch toolchain, because it is genuinely ours:
# mesa-patches/ applies to a specific tree, and a Mesa that moved
# underneath would break Phase 3 silently rather than loudly.
#
# Moved 26.1.5 -> 26.1.6 on 2026-08-10: a point release inside the
# pinned series, "New features: None", 26 bug fixes and no NVK change
# outside src/nouveau/vulkan/nvk_{cmd_buffer,shader}.c — neither of
# which mesa-patches/ touches. The series applies unchanged, 75 of 75.
# https://docs.mesa3d.org/relnotes/26.1.6.html
#
# Moved 26.1.6 -> 26.1.7 on 2026-08-16: also a point release inside the
# pinned series, "New features: None", 89 commits closing 13 reported
# issues. Unlike the last one it DOES touch six of the 121 files
# mesa-patches/ writes to, and the series still applies 77 of 77 with no
# fuzz and no rejects. Taken for one reason above the rest: "nak:
# Serialize carry access in instr_sched_prepass" is a fix on the
# Maxwell path — SM50 has exactly one carry register (sm50.rs:73) and
# the pre-Volta 64-bit add lowering uses it (builder.rs:414), so the
# unserialised prepass could overlap two carry live ranges.
# https://docs.mesa3d.org/relnotes/26.1.7.html
#
# The 26.2 series (26.2.0, 2026-08-05) is deliberately NOT taken here:
# it is a new development series whose own release notes say to stick
# with a previous release for stability, and it moves NVK substantially
# (mesh shaders, shader_atomic_float, display timing). Taking it is a
# decision, not an update — R14/D2 territory, recorded as D21. Re-checked
# 2026-08-16: still no 26.2.1, so there is nothing new to weigh.
#
#   git ls-remote --tags https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa.git mesa-26.1.7
MESA_REPO=https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa.git
MESA_TAG=mesa-26.1.7

# The commit the tag points at. This is what scripts/fetch-mesa.sh
# verifies; the tag alone is not enough, since tags can be moved.
MESA_COMMIT=e8617e4ca95fc655b0f13fd115c224d27eba2441
MESA_TAG_OBJECT=09741f24d171284a026345da95fedd31685d8dda

# Fallback when git-over-https is blocked: GitLab serves subtree
# tarballs addressed by commit. Verified working from this environment.
MESA_ARCHIVE_BASE=https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/archive

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Meson
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mesa 26.1.7's root meson.build declares meson_version : '>= 1.4.0'
# (meson.build:9, unchanged from 26.1.5 and 26.1.6).
# The image has no meson at all and Debian bookworm's is 1.3.2, so
# scripts/ install this version into a gitignored directory. Pinned
# because nothing in the environment supplies it — it is ours to choose.
MESON_VERSION=1.11.2

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python modules Mesa's code generators need (milestone item 6)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mesa runs these on the *build* machine to generate sources; they are
# not part of the Switch toolchain and the image ships neither them nor
# pip. Measured by configuring the pinned tree: without mako, Mesa stops
# at "Python (3.x) mako module >= 0.8.0 required to build mesa".
#
# Pinned for the same reason as Meson: nothing in the environment
# supplies them, so the choice is ours. Installed on the host — the
# container has no network — into a gitignored directory and made
# visible through PYTHONPATH.
MESA_PYTHON_MAKO_VERSION=1.3.12
MESA_PYTHON_PYYAML_VERSION=6.0.3

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# bindgen and cbindgen — build-machine tools Mesa's Rust half needs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mesa generates NAK's and NIL's C bindings with bindgen, and NIL's
# public nil.h with cbindgen. Both are *build-machine* tools, like
# Meson and mako, and nothing in the environment supplies them: the
# toolchain image has neither, and a host build of them is an Ubuntu
# binary a Debian 12 container cannot run. So they are ours to choose,
# and scripts/fetch-rust-tools.sh builds them for the toolchain.
#
# Version floors, measured against the pinned Mesa tree:
#   bindgen  >= 0.71.1, and 0.72.0 is refused as known-buggy
#            (mesa/meson.build:850-865)
#   cbindgen >= 0.28    (mesa/meson.build:909; src/nouveau/nil asks
#                        only for >= 0.25, the higher floor wins)
BINDGEN_CLI_VERSION=0.72.1
BINDGEN_CLI_SHA256=8a408c0fcb20bf7bd4ceaf4bf990e223e3543a04b84d2394f3edeee29a0e87e2
CBINDGEN_VERSION=0.29.4
CBINDGEN_SHA256=2ecb53484c9c167ba674026b656d8a27d7657a58e6066aa902bfb1a4aa00ae20

# libclang, which bindgen dlopens at run time rather than linking.
#
# It has to be a *Debian bookworm* build, because that is what the
# toolchain image is (measured: glibc 2.36) and bindgen runs inside it.
# The host here is Ubuntu 24.04 with glibc 2.39, so its own
# libclang-18 is not usable there.
#
# Two packages, not one: libclang1-16 declares
#   Depends: libc6 (>= 2.34), libgcc-s1, libllvm16, libstdc++6 (>= 11)
# and readelf confirms NEEDED libLLVM-16.so.1. The other three are
# already in the image. Nothing else from either package is extracted.
DEBIAN_LIBCLANG_URL=http://deb.debian.org/debian/pool/main/l/llvm-toolchain-16
DEBIAN_LIBCLANG_DEB=libclang1-16_16.0.6-15~deb12u1_amd64.deb
DEBIAN_LIBCLANG_SHA256=eb479490768a60599896a525825387264987325df6fbefbc090aeeac56843a39
DEBIAN_LIBLLVM_DEB=libllvm16_16.0.6-15~deb12u1_amd64.deb
DEBIAN_LIBLLVM_SHA256=ba0b6f4a348373d82e8c180c8f94ea5e9f0227afe4e01c78e5a66ec71fd2df1e
# Paths *inside* those .deb archives, and the sonames they carry.
DEBIAN_LIBCLANG_MEMBER=./usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libclang-16.so.16.0.6
DEBIAN_LIBLLVM_MEMBER=./usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libLLVM-16.so.1
DEBIAN_LIBLLVM_SONAME=libLLVM-16.so.1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# mesa_clc — the OpenCL-C compiler NVK needs at build time
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# NVK compiles src/nouveau/vulkan/cl/*.cl into SPIR-V during the build
# and turns the result into C++ (query-pool copies, indirect copies).
# mesa/meson.build puts with_nouveau_vk in `with_driver_using_cl`
# unconditionally, so there is no configuration of NVK that skips it.
#
# mesa_clc is a build-machine tool and needs LLVM, clang,
# SPIRV-LLVM-Translator, SPIRV-Tools and libclc. scripts/fetch-clc-deps.sh
# fetches them on the host; toolchain/Dockerfile installs and builds them.
#
# LLVM **15**, not the 16 already in the image for libclang: Mesa
# requires an SPIRV-LLVM-Translator matching the chosen LLVM's
# major.minor (mesa/meson.build:2030-2042), and bookworm packages
# libllvmspirvlib for 14 and 15 only. Fifteen means every piece comes
# from the distribution.
DEBIAN_MIRROR=http://deb.debian.org/debian
DEBIAN_SUITE=bookworm
# Roots of the dependency closure; scripts/fetch-clc-deps.sh resolves
# the rest against what the base image already has.
DEBIAN_CLC_PACKAGES="llvm-15-dev clang-15 libclang-15-dev libclang-cpp15-dev libclc-15-dev libllvmspirvlib-15-dev zlib1g-dev libzstd-dev libexpat1-dev"

# SPIRV-Tools is the one piece bookworm cannot supply: Mesa requires
# >= 2024.1 (mesa/meson.build:2054) and bookworm ships 2023.1. Built in
# the image from this tag.
#
# Fetched with `git clone --depth 1`, not as a release tarball:
# codeload.github.com answers 403 through this environment's egress
# proxy while git-over-https is allowed. Measured, and it is the same
# split scripts/fetch-mesa.sh already handles for GitLab.
SPIRV_TOOLS_REPO=https://github.com/KhronosGroup/SPIRV-Tools.git
SPIRV_TOOLS_TAG=v2024.4
SPIRV_TOOLS_COMMIT=4d2f0b40bfe290dea6c6904dafdf7fd8328ba346
# SPIRV-Tools does not build without SPIRV-Headers, and pins the
# revision it wants in its own DEPS file. This is that revision, read
# from the tag above rather than chosen here.
SPIRV_HEADERS_REPO=https://github.com/KhronosGroup/SPIRV-Headers.git
SPIRV_HEADERS_COMMIT=3f17b2af6784bfa2c5aa5dbb8e0e74a607dd8b3b

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Rust target (docs/rust-toolchain.md, R13)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# rustc already ships this target (tier 3, os = "horizon", std = false,
# panic = abort). We do NOT define a custom one.
#
# toolchain/aarch64-horizon.json snapshots its spec. That is a tripwire,
# not a pin: the target definition decides how NAK/NIL get compiled, so
# a silent change to its panic strategy or feature set should show up as
# a diff. Precisely because the environment's nightly floats,
# scripts/check-rust-target.sh reports drift and exits 0 by default.
RUST_TARGET=aarch64-nintendo-switch-freestanding

# No Rust std sysroot is built. R13 was investigated against the Mesa
# tree at MESA_COMMIT before any toolchain work: NAK/NIL need `std` as
# Mesa links them today, but the gap to no_std+alloc is a handful of
# mechanical substitutions, deferred to mesa-patches/ in Phase 3/4.
RUST_BUILD_STD=no
